From: Venus CF4 <cf4@localhost>
Date: Sat, 12 Sep 2026 15:20:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] media: venus: report exact IRIS1 encoder capture size

After the IRIS1 encoder starts using firmware's compressed-output requirement
as the authoritative CAPTURE allocation size, G_FMT must report that same
negotiated size for an allocated CAPTURE queue. The older max() rule now
re-inflates firmware's 230400-byte requirement to the generic 1843200-byte
estimate and contradicts QUERYBUF.

Keep the raw OUTPUT side conservative, where the Venus raw-frame layout can
legitimately exceed firmware's minimum, but report the cached firmware-backed
CAPTURE allocation exactly once the queue is busy. This mirrors downstream's
stored CAPTURE plane size and restores G_FMT/REQBUFS/QUERYBUF consistency
without relaxing userspace validation.

Signed-off-by: Venus CF4 <cf4@localhost>
---
--- a/drivers/media/platform/qcom/venus/venc.c
+++ b/drivers/media/platform/qcom/venus/venc.c
@@ -335,10 +335,11 @@
 
 	if (IS_IRIS1(inst->core) &&
 	    vb2_is_busy(v4l2_m2m_get_vq(inst->m2m_ctx, f->type))) {
-		u32 size = V4L2_TYPE_IS_OUTPUT(f->type) ? inst->input_buf_size :
-							      inst->output_buf_size;
-
-		pixmp->plane_fmt[0].sizeimage = max(pixmp->plane_fmt[0].sizeimage, size);
+		if (V4L2_TYPE_IS_OUTPUT(f->type))
+			pixmp->plane_fmt[0].sizeimage =
+				max(pixmp->plane_fmt[0].sizeimage, inst->input_buf_size);
+		else
+			pixmp->plane_fmt[0].sizeimage = inst->output_buf_size;
 	}
 
 	return 0;
